## ECC agents and stack guidance

Read `.nonoise/ecc/index.md` for the installed agents, skills and rule paths; `nonoise.config.json` records the selected stack. Read all common rules and the language rules matching the files being changed. Claude discovers `.claude/agents/` and `.claude/rules/ecc/`; Copilot discovers `.github/agents/*.agent.md` and `.github/instructions/*.instructions.md`; Codex discovers `.codex/agents/*.toml` and follows the rule links in this index. Skills live in `.claude/skills/` and, for Codex/Copilot, `.agents/skills/`.

Before delivery use the installed review agents listed in the index (test, security, silent-failure and language reviews as available). Pair `verification-loop` with `superpowers:verification-before-completion`. Use only capabilities listed in the index; if agent delegation is unavailable, apply the instructions directly and report that independent review did not run. ECC is a pinned MIT snapshot, updated manually by NONoise; no ECC plugin or hooks are required.

